*).env file is to store secrets. we are storing api keys. this will not push the secrets to github
*)we install python dotenv and change the code to get the secrets from env file
*)docker command to run the application: 
    docker build -t news-app .
    docker run -p 8501:8501 --env-file .env news-app
*)app.py is to access the code via ui (web application)
    streamlit run app.py
*)fetch-news.py is to access the code via terminal
    python src/fetch-news.py
*) below is the project structure
User enters "AWS"
      ↓
NewsAPI
      ↓
fetch_news.py
      ↓
DataFrame
      ↓
sentiment.py
      ↓
Positive / Negative / Neutral
      ↓
visualize.py
      ↓
Charts in Streamlit

